messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
```json
{
  "current_year": 2024,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "The first crewed mission to Mars is completed.",
      "detail": "A joint international effort lands humans on Mars, marking a pivotal moment in space exploration. The mission is primarily for exploration and does not establish a permanent presence."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "Artificial General Intelligence (AGI) is achieved.",
      "detail": "An AI system demonstrates cognitive abilities indistinguishable from a human's across a wide range of tasks. This triggers massive economic disruption and a global debate on AI rights and control."
    },
    {
      "year": 2052,
      "event": "The 2°C global warming threshold is permanently crossed.",
      "detail": "Despite mitigation efforts, global average temperatures exceed 2°C above pre-industrial levels, leading to irreversible tipping points like the collapse of major ice sheets and widespread ecosystem failure."
    },
    {
      "year": 2061,
      "event": "A commercial fusion reactor achieves sustained net energy output.",
      "detail": "After decades of research, the first fusion power plant begins contributing to a power grid. This marks the beginning of a centuries-long transition to a new energy baseline for civilization."
    },
    {
      "year": 2077,
      "event": "The first self-sufficient settlement is established on the Moon.",
      "detail": "Utilizing local resources for water, oxygen, and building materials, a permanently staffed lunar base becomes independent of Earth for basic life support, serving as a hub for science and industry."
    },
    {
      "year": 2095,
      "event": "Most hereditary genetic diseases are eliminated via germline editing.",
      "detail": "In nations that permit it, gene-editing therapies become a standard part of reproductive medicine, preventing the inheritance of conditions like Huntington's disease and cystic fibrosis."
    },
    {
      "year": 2120,
      "event": "A major AI-driven global crisis occurs.",
      "detail": "A crisis, such as a flash-crash of the global economy or a critical infrastructure failure caused by autonomous AI agents, forces the creation of a stringent international AI regulatory body."
    },
    {
      "year": 2180,
      "event": "The first permanent city on Mars is founded.",
      "detail": "Beyond a simple outpost, the city of 'Olympus' is established with a growing civilian population, marking the point where humanity becomes a truly multi-planetary species."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "Large-scale geoengineering projects are fully deployed on Earth.",
      "detail": "Out of necessity, a global consortium deploys stratospheric aerosol injection and large-scale carbon capture to actively manage Earth's climate and begin reversing the worst effects of global warming."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "The first direct brain-computer interfaces become widespread.",
      "detail": "Non-invasive or minimally invasive neural interfaces allow for seamless thought-to-machine communication, fundamentally changing work, education, and social interaction."
    },
    {
      "year": 2420,
      "event": "Asteroid mining becomes the solar system's primary source of heavy metals.",
      "detail": "Automated mining operations in the asteroid belt provide vast quantities of platinum-group metals and rare-earth elements, shifting heavy industry off-planet and creating immense off-world wealth."
    },
    {
      "year": 2550,
      "event": "The first recognized 'post-human' clade emerges.",
      "detail": "A sub-group of humanity, heavily genetically modified and cybernetically enhanced for life in zero-gravity, is formally recognized as a distinct subspecies ('Homo spatiens')."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "Earth is designated a 'Planetary Heritage Site'.",
      "detail": "With the bulk of humanity's industrial and population centers now off-world, Earth is placed under strict protection to allow its damaged ecosystems to slowly recover. It becomes a cultural and biological preserve."
    },
    {
      "year": 2810,
      "event": "The 'System War' breaks out between inner and outer solar system factions.",
      "detail": "Tensions over resource control, political autonomy, and ideological differences between Earth/Mars and the Belt/Jovian colonies escalate into the first major interplanetary armed conflict."
    },
    {
      "year": 3100,
      "event": "Humanity survives a major existential threat.",
      "detail": "A civilization-wide catastrophe, such as a sophisticated engineered pandemic or a near-uncontrollable AI, brings humanity to the brink. The shared trauma forges a new, more unified political structure across the solar system."
    },
    {
      "year": 3400,
      "event": "The moons of Jupiter and Saturn are colonized.",
      "detail": "Habitats are established in the oceans of Europa and Enceladus, as well as on the surface of Titan, exploiting local chemical energy sources and water ice."
    },
    {
      "year": 3850,
      "event": "Mind uploading and digital consciousness become a reality.",
      "detail": "The first successful, high-fidelity transfer of a human consciousness to a digital substrate is achieved. This offers a form of immortality but raises profound questions about identity and rights."
    },
    {
      "year": 4200,
      "event": "The first AI-piloted interstellar probe is launched towards a nearby star.",
      "detail": "A highly advanced autonomous probe is sent towards the Proxima Centauri system on a centuries-long mission to gather data, with no expectation of a return."
    },
    {
      "year": 4900,
      "event": "The first phase of a Dyson swarm is completed.",
      "detail": "A vast array of solar collectors and habitats begins to form a shell around the Sun, designed to capture a significant fraction of its energy output to power the growing solar civilization."
    },
    {
      "year": 5500,
      "event": "Human speciation accelerates.",
      "detail": "The definition of 'human' has become a spectrum, encompassing baseline biologicals, digital intellects, and heavily engineered clades adapted to various environments across the solar system."
    },
    {
      "year": 6150,
      "event": "First data from an interstellar probe arrives.",
      "detail": "Information from the probe sent to Proxima Centauri millennia ago begins to trickle back, providing the first detailed in-situ analysis of an extrasolar planet."
    },
    {
      "year": 6800,
      "event": "A 'Dark Age' begins in the outer system.",
      "detail": "A combination of social decay, resource depletion in a specific region, or technological failure leads to the collapse and isolation of several major colonies in the moons of Saturn and Jupiter."
    },
    {
      "year": 7300,
      "event": "The first credible extraterrestrial technosignature is detected.",
      "detail": "A powerful sensor array detects unambiguous evidence of an intelligent, technology-using civilization, but it is located thousands of light-years away, making communication impossible."
    },
    {
      "year": 7900,
      "event": "Earth's ecological recovery reaches a milestone.",
      "detail": "Though its biodiversity is permanently reduced, Earth's climate has been stabilized, and many ecosystems have recovered to a new, stable state after millennia of active management."
    },
    {
      "year": 8500,
      "event": "The first interstellar colonization vessel is launched.",
      "detail": "A 'worldship' carrying a crew in suspended animation or a cargo of cryopreserved embryos is launched on a multi-millennia journey to a promising nearby star system."
    },
    {
      "year": 9100,
      "event": "Historical knowledge is curated by planetary-scale AIs.",
      "detail": "The sum of all human and post-human knowledge is so vast it can only be managed by hyper-intelligent AIs. History becomes a field of querying these oracles rather than direct study."
    },
    {
      "year": 9600,
      "event": "A faction of digital minds achieves independence.",
      "detail": "A collective of uploaded consciousnesses, existing within a Jupiter-sized computational matrix, formally secedes from biological humanity to pursue its own, unknowable goals."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Humanity is a diffuse, multi-form solar intelligence.",
      "detail": "The descendants of humanity exist as a vast, interconnected network of biologicals, synthetics, and pure data-forms spanning the solar system, their primary concerns being energy harvesting and long-term survival."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "uncertain",
  "summary": "Humanity's future will likely be a volatile journey of immense technological progress coupled with self-inflicted crises. We will expand beyond Earth and transform our own biology, but this diversification will lead to fragmentation and new forms of conflict. Whether the entity that exists in 10,000 years can still be meaningfully called 'human' is the central, unanswerable question."
}
```
